meta {
  name: Connect (WS)
  type: ws
  seq: 1
}

ws {
  url: {{wsUrl}}/ws?token={{token}}
}

docs {
  # Connect (WS)

  Opens the gameplay WebSocket, authenticated via the `?token=` query
  parameter (Player 1's token by default — duplicate this request and swap
  in `{{token2}}` for Player 2).

  **Bruno's native WebSocket request support varies by version** (added
  fairly recently, and the message-sending UI/format has changed across
  releases) — this request is provided as a best effort for versions that
  support `type: ws`. If your Bruno version doesn't render a "send frame"
  box, or the connection just doesn't work, use `scripts/ws_smoke.go`
  instead (see the top-level README's "WebSocket testing" section) — it
  exercises the exact same protocol without depending on Bruno's WS support
  at all.

  Once connected (with either this request or ws_smoke.go), send these
  frames in order to replay the walkthrough in `docs/WS_EVENTS.md`:

  1. `{"type":"room.join","data":{"room_id":"{{roomId}}"}}`
  2. (owner only) `{"type":"round.start"}`
  3. `{"type":"bet.place","data":{"choice":"even","amount":1000}}`

  You should see `room.state`, then `round.started`, then `bet.accepted`,
  then (after the betting window closes) `round.result` and
  `balance.updated` arrive unprompted.
}
